---
source: crates/gitea-core/src/error/render.rs
expression: "snap(ErrorKind::KeyringUnavailable { cause: KeyringCause::NoBackend },\nRequestCtx::default())"
---
error: OS keyring is unavailable

  cause: no credential backend answered (on Linux, usually no D-Bus session)

what to do:
  unlock or enable the keyring, or use one of these alternatives:
  1. gea auth login --host git.example.org --insecure-storage  (a 0600 file)
  2. GEA_TOKEN=<token> gea auth status  (environment only)
  note: set GEA_CREDENTIAL_STORE to env, file, or keyring to select a
        storage backend.
